---
import LegalLayout from '~/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '~/config/site';

// Static content — no per-request logic — so it's served straight from
// Cloudflare's edge assets layer with zero Worker invocation.
export const prerender = true;
---

<LegalLayout
  title={`About — ${site.name}`}
  description="Why Khoobsurati exists: a small, independent 90s Bollywood radio built to feel like the neighbourhood parlour."
>
  <h1>About Khoobsurati</h1>

  <p>
    Every neighbourhood parlour had the same radio, tuned to the same station,
    playing the same handful of 90s Bollywood songs on loop — background
    music for head massages, mehndi, and gossip over chai. Khoobsurati
    (<em>खूबसूरती</em>) tries to rebuild that exact feeling: one curated
    playlist, always playing, no menu to browse.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    A single looping playlist of 90s Bollywood tracks that plays in your
    browser, with the same songs also linked out to
    <a href={site.spotifyPlaylistUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Spotify</a> and
    <a href={site.ytMusicPlaylistUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Music</a>
    if you'd rather listen there. The "online now" counter is a small
    illusion — everyone who has the page open right now is, roughly, hearing
    the same song at the same time, like a shared radio station rather than
    separate on-demand streams.
  </p>

  <h2>What it isn't</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati isn't a company, a streaming service, or a business. There's
    no sign-up, no account, no algorithm, and nothing for sale. It's a small,
    independent hobby project built and maintained by one person who missed
    this specific kind of background noise.
  </p>

  <h2>Rights &amp; credit</h2>
  <p>
    Khoobsurati doesn't host any audio itself — playback happens through
    YouTube's own embedded player, and the playlist links point to Spotify
    and YouTube Music. All songs, artists, film titles, and album art belong
    to their respective rights holders. See the
    <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Found a wrong song, a broken link, or just want to say the chai's good?
    <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
